<!--
  WreckedMachines — restoration research, WRECKED_MACHINES_RESURRECTION_1.

  Ruling this implements: canon.yml wrecked_machines (owner, 2026-08-31) says
  "restoration rows live in THE SHIP tree (Rekko-neutral register)" — a
  registration this mod owns, separate from VFE-Factory's own vanilla
  VFE_BasicFactories gate (which stays completely untouched, per
  the wrecked_machines_resurrection design doc, item 5: "the shipped state
  keeps VFE-Factory's building untouched; the ship-or-retexture question
  re-opens only after the pilot loop survives a live round").

  ⚠️ RESEARCH_TREE_NORMALIZATION_1 has NOT executed yet ("after the droids
  land", research_tree_taxonomy.md header). No ResearchTabDef named "THE SHIP"
  exists in any loaded def today — the taxonomy doc's tab column is a planned
  future categorization, not a live def. Inventing a <tab> reference to a def
  that does not exist would be a load error. Instead this project carries the
  same <tags><li>ShipRelated</li></tags> vanilla's own ShipResearchProjectBase
  uses (Data/Core/Defs/ResearchProjectDefs/ResearchProjects_5_Ship.xml) — the
  live, real convention for "this belongs to the ship cluster" — so the
  normalization pass picks this def up automatically by content match, the
  same way it already sweeps VFE_Manufacturing and the VGE systems rows
  (research_manifest_draft.csv, all tagged "Ship tree: ... swept in by
  content match"). When normalization executes and a real ResearchTabDef
  exists, add <tab> here; do not guess its defName now.

  Tier: T2 Forge by research_tree_taxonomy.md §2/§7 (late-Industrial cost
  band 1600-3000, techLevel Industrial) — this is applied bodge-science
  on ship-original systems, not the ship's own Spacer engineering.

  🔴 TECHPRINT GATE — genuine design fork, not resolved here. The resurrection
  spec (wrecked_machines_resurrection design doc, item 2) says "the
  techprint gate is the ruled faction-held access class." Investigated by
  TECHPRINT_FACTION_GATING_1 (infrastructure/state/items/
  TECHPRINT_FACTION_GATING_1.md): the faction-held mechanism itself is real
  and pure-XML (ResearchProjectDef.heldByFactionCategoryTags +
  StockGenerator_Techprints on a trader), but is BLOCKED — no design doc maps
  ANY of the 12 campaign factions to a tech-alignment domain, and that item's
  own brief says not to invent the mapping. This project therefore ships
  WITHOUT techprintCount/heldByFactionCategoryTags — no techprint gate at
  all, faction or otherwise. It is reachable by the RR Analyse study loop
  (primary route) or by RR's own bench-theory overflow (slow fallback,
  player-setting-dependent), per DESIGN.md §2's already-ratified mechanism.
  Do NOT add a techprint requirement here by guessing a faction — when
  TECHPRINT_FACTION_GATING_1 unblocks, revisit this def specifically.
-->
<Defs>

  <ResearchProjectDef>
    <defName>RM_WM_AutomatedSmelterRestoration</defName>
    <label>automated smelter restoration</label>
    <description>Study the wrecked automated smelter closely enough to understand how to rebuild it. This is not the smelter's original engineering — its makers already solved that — it is the colony's own accumulated, bodged, hard-won knowledge of how to bring a dead one back.\n\nStudying the wreck itself (Research Reinvented's Analyse) is the fast, primary route. Working it out from theory alone at a bench is possible but slow, and stays slow on purpose.</description>
    <baseCost>2000</baseCost>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <tags>
      <li>ShipRelated</li>
    </tags>
    <!-- Off in open space, deliberately away from vanilla's Ship cluster
         (X 19-22) and Main-tab crowding near the origin — cosmetic only,
         revisit once a real research-tab layout exists. -->
    <researchViewX>26</researchViewX>
    <researchViewY>12</researchViewY>
    <generalRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>subject->the automated smelter's dead circuitry</li>
        <li>subject_gerund->restoring wrecked ship machinery</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </generalRules>
  </ResearchProjectDef>

  <!-- Mobile-structure restoration (the grade-ladder extension, 2026-09-15).
       Each gates its line's REFURBISHED grade; Kludged needs no research.
       Spacer tech: these are archotech-sourced machines. Same no-techprint
       stance as the smelter project above. Studying the wreck (RR Analyse,
       SpecialResearchOpportunities_WreckedMachines.xml) is the primary route. -->
  <ResearchProjectDef>
    <defName>RM_WM_PowerCellRestoration</defName>
    <label>power cell restoration</label>
    <description>Study a wrecked vanometric power cell closely enough to restore most of its lattice. Nobody understands how the cell makes power; this is only how to stop it losing so much of it.\n\nStudying the wreck itself (Research Reinvented's Analyse) is the fast, primary route.</description>
    <baseCost>2500</baseCost>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <researchViewX>26</researchViewX>
    <researchViewY>13</researchViewY>
  </ResearchProjectDef>

  <ResearchProjectDef>
    <defName>RM_WM_EmanatorRestoration</defName>
    <label>emanator restoration</label>
    <description>Study a wrecked psychic emanator closely enough to steady its field. The principle is beyond anyone; the repair is only careful copying of what survived.\n\nStudying the wreck itself (Research Reinvented's Analyse) is the fast, primary route.</description>
    <baseCost>2500</baseCost>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <researchViewX>26</researchViewX>
    <researchViewY>14</researchViewY>
  </ResearchProjectDef>

  <!-- THE ALLOY FORGE ABOARD, SHIP_ALLOY_FORGE_1 (owner 2026-10-09, typed:
       "Yes, I think we will need an alloy forge. Maybe even earlier, but the
       recipies will unlock later in the game for more difficult alloys.
       Durasteel earlier, plasteel later..."). Spec:
       design/RimMandrake/canon_materials_design_2026-10-09.md §3.4.

       The building is VFE Factory's VFEFactory_AutomatedAlloyForge. Its stock
       gate (VFE_ComplexFactories, after Fabrication) is replaced by the early
       project below, which follows the smelter restoration: the forge comes
       right after the smelter. Its first alloy (durasteel, added by the
       RimStarWars Armoury, mandrake.rsw.armoury) needs nothing more than the
       forge. Plasteel needs the late project below.
       Patch: Patches/WreckedMachines_AlloyForgeGates.xml. Toggles:
       WreckedMachinesSettings.alloyForgeProgressiveGate / plasteelAlloyEnabled.

       ⚠️ PROVISIONAL numbers (no calibration, no ruling): both baseCosts and the
       late project's AdvancedFabrication prerequisite. -->
  <ResearchProjectDef>
    <defName>RM_WM_AlloyForgeRestoration</defName>
    <label>alloy forge restoration</label>
    <description>Bring the ship's alloy forge back to heat. Once the smelter runs, the forge is the next furnace down the line: it bonds refined metal with a hardening mineral into tougher alloys.\n\nRestoring it unlocks the forge and its first, easiest alloys. Harder alloys need further study.</description>
    <baseCost>1500</baseCost>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <prerequisites>
      <li>RM_WM_AutomatedSmelterRestoration</li>
    </prerequisites>
    <tags>
      <li>ShipRelated</li>
    </tags>
    <researchViewX>27</researchViewX>
    <researchViewY>12</researchViewY>
    <generalRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>subject->the alloy forge's cold crucibles</li>
        <li>subject_gerund->restoring the ship's alloy forge</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </generalRules>
  </ResearchProjectDef>

  <ResearchProjectDef>
    <defName>RM_WM_PlasteelAlloying</defName>
    <label>plasteel alloying</label>
    <description>Learn to drive the restored alloy forge hard enough to fuse plasteel: steel, chemfuel and a trace of gold under heat and pressure the forge was built for and has not reached in a lifetime.\n\nUnlocks the forge's plasteel recipe, the only way the colony can make plasteel itself.</description>
    <baseCost>4000</baseCost>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <prerequisites>
      <li>RM_WM_AlloyForgeRestoration</li>
      <li>AdvancedFabrication</li>
    </prerequisites>
    <tags>
      <li>ShipRelated</li>
    </tags>
    <researchViewX>28</researchViewX>
    <researchViewY>12</researchViewY>
    <generalRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>subject->plasteel fusion</li>
        <li>subject_gerund->alloying plasteel</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </generalRules>
  </ResearchProjectDef>

</Defs>
